# .oxlint-rules.txt is generated by scripts/oxlint-rules.mjs, which writes LF.
#
# Windows is the primary dev box here and has core.autocrlf=true, so without
# this git checks the file out as CRLF, the script rewrites it as LF, and it
# reads as modified forever - `git status` dirty on a clean tree, and the diff
# that is the entire point of committing the snapshot buried under line-ending
# churn. Pinning the checkout to LF makes the working tree match what the
# generator writes on every platform.
#
# Deliberately scoped to the generated file. Everything else keeps the repo's
# existing autocrlf behaviour, which has been fine.
.oxlint-rules.txt text eol=lf
